  plannedarr/.style={-{Stealth[length=2.5mm]}, thick, dashed, gray}
]
  \node[ev] (s1) {1. Event\\ingestion\\(GDELT)};
  \node[ev, right=of s1] (s2) {2. Direct\\URL join\\(GKG)};
  \node[ev, right=of s2] (s3) {3. Lexical\\candidates\\(TF-IDF/BM25)};
  \node[ev, right=of s3] (s4) {4. Rule-based\\sector labels};
  \node[an, right=of s4] (s5) {5. Market\\event window\\(analyst basket)};
  \draw[arr] (s1) -- (s2);
  \draw[arr] (s2) -- (s3);
  \draw[arr] (s3) -- (s4);
  \draw[arr] (s4) -- (s5);
  \node[planned, below=12mm of s2] (p1) {Planned temporal analysis\\(Toda--Yamamoto Granger; not run)};
  \node[planned, right=of p1] (p2) {Planned input--output propagation\\(Leontief; not run)};
  \draw[plannedarr] (p1) -- (p2);
  \node[above=2mm of s3, font=\scriptsize, align=center] {Evaluated historical replay};
  \node[below=2mm of p1, font=\scriptsize, align=center] {No validated time-series panel};
  \node[below=2mm of p2, font=\scriptsize, align=center] {No empirical input--output shocks};
\end{tikzpicture}
\caption{Evidence status of the workflow. Blue stages were exercised in the historical replay across all six cases. The orange market stage uses researcher-defined baskets and does not establish automated exposure identification. Gray dashed boxes show planned methods that were not run and produced no results for these cases. A geographic propagation map (Section~\ref{sec:propmap}) summarises the event-origin $\to$ affected-countries $\to$ India-outcome chain per case.}
\label{fig:pipeline}
\end{figure*}

The architecture is intended to support future live monitoring, but the results in this paper cover only the historical replay stages shown in blue and orange in Figure~\ref{fig:pipeline}. Streaming latency, uptime, analyst utility, and live reliability were not measured.

\subsection{Planned methods not evaluated}

The broader architecture also proposes temporal analysis and cross-sector propagation, but neither method was run for these cases. The planned temporal component includes Toda--Yamamoto Granger-predictive analysis; no validated event--market time-series panel or corresponding result was produced. The planned propagation component uses a Leontief input--output framework; no empirical input--output coefficient matrix paired with validated event shocks was available for this evaluation. These methods are therefore presented as future components of the architecture, not as methods or findings of the present study.

\subsection{Design principles}

Three principles shape the prototype and the way its outputs are reported.
\emph{Provenance first:} every linked record retains the source URL and the stage that produced the link, so an analyst can inspect why two records were connected.
\emph{Evidence-type separation:} outputs are labeled by what they can support (Table~\ref{tab:evidence}); a source-identity join is never presented as a relevance judgment, and a market estimate on an analyst-selected basket is never presented as exposure identification.
\emph{Explicit failure reporting:} unlabeled candidates (Unknown sector) and retrieval misses are reported as results rather than filtered out.

\begin{table*}[t]
\centering
\caption{Evidence types produced by the replay and what each can and cannot support.}
\label{tab:evidence}
\small
\begin{tabular}{p{3.0cm}p{6.0cm}p{7.2cm}}
\toprule
\textbf{Output} & \textbf{Supports} & \textbf{Does not support} \\
\midrule
Normalized URL match & Two records refer to the same source URL; provenance & Article relevance, accuracy, or event-date correctness \\
Lexical candidate (TF-IDF/BM25) & Retrieval by metadata overlap & Semantic relevance or event--article correctness \\
Rule-based sector label & Coverage of deterministic rules & Validated event-to-sector mapping \\
Market-model CAR on analyst basket & Descriptive market context around a date & Exposure identification, prediction, or causality \\
Geographic propagation map & Visual summary of pipeline reasoning chain per case & Ground-truth geographic impact or causal propagation \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table*}

