\section{Data and cases}\label{sec:data}

\subsection{Data sources}

The project archives daily GDELT event exports and GDELT GKG v1 metadata exports for 2024 Q1. GDELT event dates are media-detection dates and may differ from the dates on which underlying events occurred. GKG v1 provides metadata such as themes, named entities, locations, and tone; it does not provide full article text in this study. Market data are adjusted-close histories for the analyst-defined baskets and benchmarks listed in Section~\ref{sec:methods}, obtained from Yahoo Finance using \texttt{yfinance}. The saved case manifests record a download date of 5 October 2026 and a requested price interval of 1 June 2023--30 April 2024.

\subsection{Case 1: Red Sea, 12 January 2024}

The first case is a Red Sea/Houthi-related sample dated 12~January 2024. It contains 30 selected GDELT event records and uses a same-day GKG corpus with 108{,}343 usable metadata rows. Selection retained 12 January records with CAMEO root code 19, source URLs matching Red Sea/Houthi/Yemen/shipping terms, actor names matching Yemen/Houthi/naval/shipping terms, and at least 10 article mentions. Duplicate source URLs were collapsed to the highest-mention record; the 30 highest-mention rows were kept.

\subsection{Case 2: Semiconductor export controls, 29 January 2024}

The second case is a 29~January 2024 BIS Export Administration Regulations update tightening US controls on advanced semiconductor equipment exported to China. Seven GDELT event-code records share the report's source URL; this represents repeated coded records linked to one article, not seven distinct articles. The same-day GKG corpus has 120{,}718 metadata rows. The primary NSE outcome is the Nifty IT index (\texttt{\^{}CNXIT}); India's channel is downstream chip scarcity pressure on automotive and AI data-centre demand.

\subsection{Cases 3--6: additional pre-registered cases}\label{sec:newcases}

Four further cases were selected under the same inclusion protocol (Table~\ref{tab:caseregistry}), each with an auditable real-world anchor, a keyword and CAMEO filter written before examining returns, and a minimum of five GDELT event records after deduplication (or one named policy document with an identifiable URL). Cases within the same stratum are at least 14 calendar days apart.

