\subsection{Summary of evidence}

Across both depth cases, direct source links retained traceability when metadata retrieval was weak. The lexical stage generated candidates, but its exact-source diagnostics were poor, and the sector rules left most Red Sea candidates unmapped. Descriptive market calculations were possible for researcher-defined baskets, but the workflow did not produce validated security exposure links. Taken together, the evidence supports a bounded historical processing demonstration and identifies retrieval and exposure mapping as unresolved stages.

