\subsection{Geographic propagation maps}\label{sec:propmap}

Figure~\ref{fig:propmap_cs01} shows the propagation map for CS-01 (Red Sea). Each map has three layers: (1)~a red star at the event's geographic origin; (2)~orange circles at the centroids of directly affected countries, sized by mean absolute Goldstein score of GDELT events near the anchor date; and (3)~a dashed arrow from the origin to India, coloured red if the event-study CAR is confirmed negative ($p<0.05$), green if confirmed positive, and grey if the result is null or unavailable. An inset panel shows the raw cumulative return at the 1/7/14/30-day horizons. Maps for all six cases are produced by \texttt{src/geosignal/visualization/propagation\_map.py} and available in the repository under \texttt{results/figures/<case\_id>/propagation\_map.png}.

The maps visualise the pipeline's reasoning chain---which countries the pipeline treated as exposed and what market response it measured---and are not claims about actual geographic impact. The caption on each figure reads: ``Pipeline-detected propagation pathway (GDELT-sourced $\cdot$ indicative only).''

