\section{Sector rules and proxy-basket membership}\label{app:taxonomy}

The configured mapper uses keyword rules in the GICS taxonomy. Examples are oil/crude/LNG for Energy; shipping/freight/logistics/Suez for Industrials; rice/wheat/food for Consumer Staples; and semiconductor/chip/EUV/NAND for Information Technology. A candidate is labeled Unknown if no configured rule matches. These rules measure text-rule coverage only; they are not validated event-to-company exposures.

